  "notes": "Labels use GPIO names from the diagram callouts; board silkscreen spellings (Rst, Bat, USB, 24, MO, MI, PCS, 7, 4...) put first in functions where they differ, followed by the CircuitPython name. LED (GPIO7) and NEOPIXEL (GPIO21) are internal and skipped. The HSTX 22-pin FPC port is skipped: the diagram lists 14 signal names (CKN, CKP, D0N, D0P, D1N, D1P, D2N, D2P, D11, D10, SCL, SDA, 3.3V, GND) but the leader lines do not map them to individual contact positions. Left-side silkscreen between Rst and GND shows a single 3.3V marking for the two 3.3V pins."
